{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-18T19:11:37.555Z","data":{"text":"Task 3 is complete. Summary of what changed:\n\n**`tests/package-install-smoke.test.ts`**\n- Removed the `before` hook (and `before` import); workspace creation, build, pack, `npm init`, and tarball install now run inside the first `it`, renamed `packs and installs the local tarball into an isolated temporary project`.\n- `workDir`/`consumerDir`/`tarballPath` stay suite-scoped; added a `setupComplete` flag. The remaining `it` blocks start with `assert.ok(setupComplete, 'Smoke test setup did not complete')`.\n- `run()` wraps spawn failures and rethrows `Command failed: <cmd> <args> (cwd: <cwd>)` plus stderr/message.\n- Added a test-only `OSQ_SMOKE_TARBALL` override so the reporting test can force a nonexistent tarball without mutating a copy of the file.\n\n**`tests/smoke-error-reporting.test.ts`** (new)\n- Spawns the smoke test with `--test-reporter=tap` and a missing tarball, strips `NODE_TEST_CONTEXT` (otherwise the child refuses to run), and asserts `not ok`, the command/args/cwd details, `# cancelled 0`, and no `cancelledByParent`.\n\n**Verification**\n- `node --import tsx --test tests/smoke-error-reporting.test.ts` → 1 pass, 0 cancelled.\n- Direct failure run shows `not ok` naming `npm install … --prefer-offline (cwd: …/consumer)` with `# cancelled 0`; later tests fail cleanly rather than being cancelled.\n- Normal smoke test 3/3 pass; package-hygiene 4/4 pass; `tsc --noEmit` clean; biome clean on both files.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/019-pack-smoke-test-fix/.run/results/3.md`."}}
